2026-03-31 01:57:56 - Agent_20260331015225 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 5 CodeQL queries covering SpEL template injection in Spring Boot Admin notifiers and Hazelcast deserialization. Found a consistent pattern across 8 notifiers (SlackNotifier, DingTalkNotifier, DiscordNotifier, HipchatNotifier, TelegramNotifier, LetsChatNotifier, OpsGenieNotifier, PagerdutyNotifier) and MicrosoftTeamsNotifier where: (1) configuration properties bound via @ConfigurationProperties parse string values directly into SpEL template expressions using SpelExpressionParser, (2) these expressions are evaluated using unrestricted StandardEvaluationContext (not SimpleEvaluationContext), allowing full SpEL capabilities including T(java.lang.Runtime).getRuntime().exec(). Exploitation requires configuration-level access (application.properties, Spring Cloud Config, or writable Actuator /env endpoint). Also flagged Hazelcast IMap EntryListener for manual review as its deserialization risk depends on Hazelcast serialization configuration. MailNotifier's Thymeleaf template processing and the MicrosoftTeamsNotifier's multiple SpEL fields were also confirmed as part of the same vulnerability pattern. Submitted 9 true positives and 1 manual review finding.
