2026-03-31 02:00:15 - Agent_20260331015225 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 9 SpEL injection findings across 9 notifier classes in spring-boot-admin-server. All findings are true positives sharing the same vulnerability pattern:

1. Each notifier has one or more SpEL Expression fields (message/description/subtitle) configurable via application.properties through @ConfigurationProperties bindings
2. The setters parse user-provided strings as SpEL template expressions using SpelExpressionParser
3. When events fire, these expressions are evaluated against an unrestricted StandardEvaluationContext (instead of the safer SimpleEvaluationContext)
4. StandardEvaluationContext allows arbitrary method invocations including T(java.lang.Runtime).getRuntime().exec() enabling RCE

Affected notifiers: SlackNotifier, DingTalkNotifier, DiscordNotifier, HipchatNotifier, LetsChatNotifier, MicrosoftTeamsNotifier, OpsGenieNotifier, PagerdutyNotifier, TelegramNotifier.

The exploitation requires write access to application.properties or a Spring Cloud Config server - making this a configuration-level SpEL injection vulnerability with medium likelihood but high impact. All 9 findings submitted as true positives.
